{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# S9 — ADR + documentation for the provider seam and the two-tier support policy\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nAfter S1–S8 rebar has a provider seam, a tier policy, a Bedrock path, and tier-stamped verdicts — none of it\nwritten down. `docs/llm-framework.md:121-143` still describes provider support as \"pydantic-ai resolves the\nprovider from the model string\" with no mention of tiers, Bedrock, or what a best-effort provider means for a\nsigned verdict, and its `:131-133` local-server recipe describes behavior that only becomes true in S4. Without\na recorded decision, the next Bedrock/gateway request reopens the same argument as a one-off, which is the\nfailure mode this epic exists to end.\n\n## Approach\n\nWrite one ADR recording the decisions and, importantly, the rejected alternatives with their evidence: the seam\nis pydantic-ai's `provider_factory` hook and capabilities come from `ModelProfile`; two support tiers with\nAnthropic and Bedrock first-class; native Bedrock rather than a gateway; LiteLLM rejected as an in-process\ndependency but reachable as a proxy; verdicts sign on every tier but stamp the tier. Then bring\n`docs/llm-framework.md` in line with what the code now does, including the Bedrock recipe, the tier table, and\nwhat tier means for an attestation consumer.\n\nThe ADR also records the two operational findings this epic turned up, so they are not rediscovered: the IMDS\nhop-limit constraint and its containment [rebar:9249-1569-7be9-4f67], and the measured relationship between\ncross-region inference profiles and prompt caching [rebar:2932-8a98-6d70-4550].\n\n**Alternative rejected:** documenting in `docs/llm-framework.md` only. That records the *what* but not the\n*why*, and rebar's ADR set is where rejected alternatives live — without them the LiteLLM and gateway options\nget re-proposed.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `docs/adr/00NN-llm-provider-seam-and-support-tiers.md` (new).\n- `docs/llm-framework.md` — the provider section (`:121-143`) and the env table (`:224-226`).\n- `docs/env-vars.md` — regenerated.\n- `README.md` — one line if the provider story is summarized there.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] the ADR exists, is `Accepted`, and names each rejected alternative (in-process LiteLLM, gateway-fronted\n      Bedrock, refuse-to-sign off-tier, Bedrock API key in SSM, cross-provider fallback) with the evidence that\n      rejected it\n- [ ] [operator-attested] every runnable command in `docs/llm-framework.md`'s provider section has been executed and produced the\n      documented result, confirmed in a ticket comment\n- [ ] the docs state, for each tier, what is guaranteed (tests, parity) and what a consumer can infer from a\n      verdict's stamped tier\n- [ ] [operator-attested] the documented generator produces NO diff to `docs/env-vars.md`, evidenced by the\n      command and its empty-diff output quoted in a comment"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785450629772744001,"uuid":"0ad12650-963f-4356-9557-99577ba9f4bc"}